---
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components';
---
<!-- Themes Section -->
<section id="themes" class="themes-section">
	<div class="container">
		<h2 class="section-title">Challenge Themes</h2>
		<p class="section-description">Choose a track and build solutions that push forward CICON's mission and help real communities</p>
		
		<div class="themes-grid">
			<div class="theme-card">
				<div class="theme-icon"><Icon name="lucide:users" /></div>
				<h3>Repair Tech for Everyone</h3>
				<p class="theme-subtitle">Bring circularity to more people by making tools simpler, more inclusive, and easier to access.</p>
				<p>Design for cobblers with limited tech, users without smartphones, or communities overlooked by mainstream platforms.</p>
			</div>
			
			<div class="theme-card">
				<div class="theme-icon"><Icon name="lucide:recycle" /></div>
				<h3>Circularity Beyond Shoes</h3>
				<p class="theme-subtitle">Tackle broader sustainability challenges by extending the life of everyday items</p>
				<p>Explore creative ways to reduce waste, track usage, or promote reuse in new categories.</p>
			</div>
			
			<div class="theme-card">
				<div class="theme-icon"><Icon name="lucide:chart-spline" /></div>
				<h3>Marketing & Visibility</h3>
				<p class="theme-subtitle">Help the right people find and care about repair.</p>
				<p>Build lightweight automated tools, campaigns, or systems that get repair in front of B2C audiences, especially people who've never considered it before.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="theme-card">
				<div class="theme-icon"><Icon name="lucide:train-track" /></div>
				<h3>Open Track</h3>
				<p class="theme-subtitle">Have something ambitious that doesn't quite fit the brief?</p>
				<p>Pitch it here, we're open to ideas that still align with circularity and CICON's mission, even if they don't match a theme directly.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>